#
# Counter-example for the closed-form gate: a math:ClosedFormFunction that declares
# its math:domain, math:codomain, and math:formalArgument but OMITS its
# math:definingExpression (sh:minCount 1, derived from the exact-one
# math:definingExpression restriction). Validation MUST emit
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (math:UnboundClosedForm). The frame and formal
# argument are present, so the missing body is the single isolated violation — a
# closed form that does not say what it computes is ill-formed. Bound by
# tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecClosedFormMissingBody).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:bodylessForm a math:ClosedFormFunction ;
    math:domain math:realNumbers ;
    math:codomain math:realNumbers ;
    math:formalArgument ex:xDecl .

ex:xDecl a math:FreeVariableDeclaration .
